outils.description:
Edit a Word document of the sandbox with a list of operations, applied together in one save. Paragraph (p), table, row and column numbers start at 0 and refer to the document BEFORE this call, as docx_read shows it:
  {op:'replace', find, replace}            everywhere, headers and tables included (exact case unless match_case:false)
  {op:'fill', values:{client:'ACME'}}       fills {{client}} placeholders
  {op:'set', p, text}                       rewrites one paragraph (style kept)
  {op:'delete', p} · {op:'delete', p, to} · {op:'delete', table}
  {op:'insert', after|before: p or heading text, content: Markdown}
  {op:'insert', at_end_of: heading text, content}
  {op:'append', content: Markdown}          at the end (charts !id allowed)
  {op:'set_cell', table, row, col, text} · {op:'add_row', table, values} · {op:'delete_row', table, row}   (from 0, row 0 = header)
  {op:'meta', title, author, subject}
save_as = write a copy instead of modifying the file. If the file changed since it was read, nothing is written (concurrent_modification): read it again.

Create a PowerPoint deck (.pptx) in the sandbox. Each slide is {layout, …}:
  title {title, subtitle, author, date} · section {title, subtitle} · agenda {items}
  bullets {title, bullets, takeaway} · two_content {title, left, right}
  kpi {title, items:[{value:'18,4 M€', label, delta:'+12 %'}]}
  chart {title, chart:'!id' from a chart_<type> tool, takeaway}
  table {title, table} · comparison {title, left:{title, items}, right:{title, items}}
  timeline {title, milestones:[{date, title}]} · process {title, steps}
  image {title, image: sandbox path} · quote {text, author} · closing {title, contact}
Every slide accepts notes (speaker notes). Layouts are composed and text is fitted for you. An existing file at path is replaced (previous version kept in the file history, up to 5 MB).

Edit a PowerPoint deck of the sandbox with a list of operations, applied together in one save. Slide numbers start at 1 and refer to the deck BEFORE this call; shape numbers come from pptx_read:
  {op:'replace', find, replace} · {op:'fill', values:{client:'ACME'}}
  {op:'set_text', slide, shape, text}     shape number from pptx_read; one line per paragraph
  {op:'add_slides', slides:[…same objects as pptx_create…], after|before: slide number}
  {op:'delete_slide', slide} · {op:'move_slide', slide, to} · {op:'duplicate_slide', slide, to?}   (to = position in the deck at that point)
  {op:'notes', slide, text} · {op:'meta', title, author}
save_as = write a copy instead of modifying the file. If the file changed since it was read, nothing is written (concurrent_modification): read it again.
